---
title: Figure 8. DocuTracker User Sequence Diagram
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor E as Employee
    participant UI as Flutter DocuTracker UI
    participant API as Express API
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    actor R as Reviewer / Signer

    E->>UI: Create or edit document draft
    UI->>API: Save document/content
    API->>DB: Validate permission and persist draft
    DB-->>API: Saved record and revision
    API-->>UI: Confirmed draft
    E->>UI: Submit document
    UI->>API: Request validated transition
    API->>DB: Validate workflow, assign reviewer,<br/>create routing/history/notification
    DB-->>API: Committed workflow state
    API-->>UI: Submitted document
    API-->>R: Assignment notification
    R->>UI: Open assigned document
    UI->>API: Request authorized document bundle
    API->>DB: Check access and load current state
    DB-->>API: Document, routing, capabilities
    API-->>UI: Authorized document details
    R->>UI: Approve, forward, return or reject
    UI->>API: Send action with idempotency key
    API->>DB: Validate assignee/action and<br/>atomically update state and audit trail
    DB-->>API: Committed result
    API-->>UI: Confirmed action and refreshed state
    API-->>E: Status notification
